TIC-TAC-TOE (INTERACTIVE)
Use terminal_send and terminal_read on persistent PTY, NOT execute_command.
At shell: text:'tictactoe' (PLAYER first) or 'tictactoe -c' (COM first),
key:'ENTER', terminal_read({}).
Default PLAYER=X first, COM=O second; -c reverses their marks. Select a 3x3 cell with arrows (or h j k l).
Use key:'SPACE' to place your mark. Columns a-c, rows 1-3.
After valid move COM responds after about 400 ms; read again,
check Turn: PLAYER before next placement. [X]/[O] is last move;
reverse video is cursor selection, not necessarily last move.
Occupied cell increments Invalid moves: PLAYER. COM uses full
search and cannot lose. r resets, preserving -c; q exits to the shared shell.
